      "title": "Scientific preprocessing is not necessarily timed work",
      "observation": "The first four Marching Cubes minmax/compaction stages are scientifically necessary and execute before the timer. Only triangle-generation family enters the selected measured closure; the source exports counts and partial coordinate summaries, not mesh arrays. A first-per-function profile can therefore contain genuine scientific preprocessing samples that are outside the primary timer. Inclusion is source membership, never proof which warmup/trial was captured.",
